(69037, 2148, 772, '<td valign="top">Interesting photo... I believe the focus on this one is a bit too soft for my taste.. I like to see detail on animals...</td>', 'Interesting photo... I believe the focus on this one is a bit too soft for my taste.. I like to see detail on animals...', '2002-06-04 00:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(69038, 2148, 1880, '<td valign="top">How did you get them to pose like that ?</td>', 'How did you get them to pose like that ?', '2002-06-04 01:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(69039, 2148, 543, '<td valign="top">Hard to tell, but I think the lighting might have been flat on the day you were shooting.  The image has been given adequate contrast overall, but the whites have mostly been soaked up by the wall in the bg, leaving the dogs looking a bit flat.  Possibly some camera shake or a focus issue, as well.  Most of the time, B/W needs to be tack sharp.</td>', 'Hard to tell, but I think the lighting might have been flat on the day you were shooting.  The image has been given adequate contrast overall, but the whites have mostly been soaked up by the wall in the bg, leaving the dogs looking a bit flat.  Possibly some camera shake or a focus issue, as well.  Most of the time, B/W needs to be tack sharp.', '2002-06-04 03:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(69040, 2148, 1031, '<td valign="top">If only one dog knew how to do a headstand! Funny idea!</td>', 'If only one dog knew how to do a headstand! Funny idea!', '2002-06-04 03:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(69041, 2148, 1175, '<td valign="top">Need more focus.  If its an attempt at "soft focus" I don'' t like it.</td>', 'Need more focus.  If its an attempt at "soft focus" I don'' t like it.', '2002-06-04 07:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(69042, 2148, 641, '<td valign="top">I like the way their head are looking different directions. I think though if the poles and sign were out of the way I''d like it more.</td>', 'I like the way their head are looking different directions. I think though if the poles and sign were out of the way I''d like it more.', '2002-06-04 16:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
