(69187, 2155, 1128, '<td valign="top">If anyone is interested... taking photos of water drops is easier than I thought it would be.  If you have a camera that you can adjust the setting manually, set it at F10 and 1/800 (the smallest "opening" and the shortest exposure time).  Then, use a slow flash and experiment with water out of a faucet until you get the photo you like.  I have found that faucets with multiple streams work the best (like a shower head and the spray nozzle on the sink).  Feel free to check the "drops" part of my website (homepage.mac.com/lianabond) and email me if you have other questions.</td>', 'If anyone is interested... taking photos of water drops is easier than I thought it would be.  If you have a camera that you can adjust the setting manually, set it at F10 and 1/800 (the smallest "opening" and the shortest exposure time).  Then, use a slow flash and experiment with water out of a faucet until you get the photo you like.  I have found that faucets with multiple streams work the best (like a shower head and the spray nozzle on the sink).  Feel free to check the "drops" part of my website (homepage.mac.com/lianabond) and email me if you have other questions.', '2002-06-10 18:03:00.000000', NULL, 0),
