(70092, 2196, 1211, '<td valign="top">Very creative.  I really like this.  (still taking it in.)  I like the focus here and the lighting a lot.</td>', 'Very creative.  I really like this.  (still taking it in.)  I like the focus here and the lighting a lot.', '2002-06-03 19:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70093, 2196, 1313, '<td valign="top">Werid but kind of cool.  At least its different.</td>', 'Werid but kind of cool.  At least its different.', '2002-06-03 20:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70094, 2196, 1831, '<td valign="top">I originally marked this as a 5 (I look at each photo then rate them on immediate impact). Having go thro the process again I realise that this image is very cleverly done and sends a greay message. well done. gets 8.</td>', 'I originally marked this as a 5 (I look at each photo then rate them on immediate impact). Having go thro the process again I realise that this image is very cleverly done and sends a greay message. well done. gets 8.', '2002-06-04 05:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70095, 2196, 641, '<td valign="top">Good shot. Not much else to say.</td>', 'Good shot. Not much else to say.', '2002-06-04 17:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70096, 2196, 1037, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure what I''m looking at... some kind of interesting sculpture, but the textures are very nice.</td>', 'I''m not sure what I''m looking at... some kind of interesting sculpture, but the textures are very nice.', '2002-06-05 11:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70097, 2196, 1897, '<td valign="top">I do not get this.</td>', 'I do not get this.', '2002-06-05 16:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70098, 2196, 1446, '<td valign="top">Not a big fan of oof objects in the forground, sorry.  I find it distracting, but this is just my oppinion.</td>', 'Not a big fan of oof objects in the forground, sorry.  I find it distracting, but this is just my oppinion.', '2002-06-06 10:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70099, 2196, 472, '<td valign="top">very odd.  creative as heck.  i like this concept. the execution could be a little better.  maybe a little more contrast in your image editor.</td>', 'very odd.  creative as heck.  i like this concept. the execution could be a little better.  maybe a little more contrast in your image editor.', '2002-06-07 00:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70100, 2196, 1597, '<td valign="top">creative but doesn''t grab my attention nice contrast</td>', 'creative but doesn''t grab my attention nice contrast', '2002-06-08 00:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70101, 2196, 875, '<td valign="top">Very creative.  I like the texture of the "wall".  I wish there was something a bit dark in the photo to balance out the midtones.</td>', 'Very creative.  I like the texture of the "wall".  I wish there was something a bit dark in the photo to balance out the midtones.', '2002-06-09 02:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70102, 2196, 543, '<td valign="top">Here''s one where an oof element in the fg doesn''t hurt (IMO).  Very good exapmle of using photography to add something to an existing artwork, and well photographed, to boot.</td>', 'Here''s one where an oof element in the fg doesn''t hurt (IMO).  Very good exapmle of using photography to add something to an existing artwork, and well photographed, to boot.', '2002-06-09 04:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70103, 2196, 1256, '<td valign="top">interesting...front figure out of focus</td>', 'interesting...front figure out of focus', '2002-06-09 15:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70104, 2196, 1078, '<td valign="top">This is a cool reinterpretation of someone else''s work.  (Don''t worry, not gonna cream you for the using someone else''s art.)  Personally, I would have pushed the forground figure a little further out of focus, but that''s me.  Mostly, I think there needs to be a simpler background -- both through the "window" and along the far right edge of the "wall".  Since I don''t know if you have access to this sculpture everyday, it may or may not be good advice to go back and have someone hold a sheet or something up to mask the background, but I''ll make the suggestion anyway.</td>', 'This is a cool reinterpretation of someone else''s work.  (Don''t worry, not gonna cream you for the using someone else''s art.)  Personally, I would have pushed the forground figure a little further out of focus, but that''s me.  Mostly, I think there needs to be a simpler background -- both through the "window" and along the far right edge of the "wall".  Since I don''t know if you have access to this sculpture everyday, it may or may not be good advice to go back and have someone hold a sheet or something up to mask the background, but I''ll make the suggestion anyway.', '2002-06-09 17:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70105, 2196, 1, '<td valign="top">Very very strange, I''d like to know what this is exactly.  I think it may be a bit bright, try workign with the levels a little.</td>', 'Very very strange, I''d like to know what this is exactly.  I think it may be a bit bright, try workign with the levels a little.', '2002-06-10 00:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70106, 2197, 1226, '<td valign="top">This one seems a bit too sharp for me. The edges are a bit too drastic. I like the overall arrangement, but the contrast does not make it feel very warm to me.</td>', 'This one seems a bit too sharp for me. The edges are a bit too drastic. I like the overall arrangement, but the contrast does not make it feel very warm to me.', '2002-06-03 02:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70107, 2197, 1, '<td valign="top">That''s a pretty extensive earring.  The composure is nice, and the background is awesome -- sadly it''s a rather bland subject.</td>', 'That''s a pretty extensive earring.  The composure is nice, and the background is awesome -- sadly it''s a rather bland subject.', '2002-06-03 13:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70108, 2197, 2, '<td valign="top">I think I''d have played with the levels of this shot, as the whole image seems to sit right around the mid-tone level.  I think pushing the dark and light tones further towards their respective poles would have made the objects stand out even further from the great texture you have.</td>', 'I think I''d have played with the levels of this shot, as the whole image seems to sit right around the mid-tone level.  I think pushing the dark and light tones further towards their respective poles would have made the objects stand out even further from the great texture you have.', '2002-06-03 14:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70109, 2197, 570, '<td valign="top">huh?</td>', 'huh?', '2002-06-03 15:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70110, 2197, 327, '<td valign="top">Neat b&amp;w.</td>', 'Neat b&w.', '2002-06-03 18:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70111, 2197, 1547, '<td valign="top">I like the different textures and shapes</td>', 'I like the different textures and shapes', '2002-06-03 20:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70112, 2197, 1031, '<td valign="top">I wish I coul see them that clearly when trying to put some together...</td>', 'I wish I coul see them that clearly when trying to put some together...', '2002-06-04 03:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70113, 2197, 878, '<td valign="top">Nice texture in this shot</td>', 'Nice texture in this shot', '2002-06-04 11:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70114, 2197, 661, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and details.</td>', 'Nice composition and details.', '2002-06-04 20:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70115, 2197, 258, '<td valign="top">Nice focus.  Good photo.</td>', 'Nice focus.  Good photo.', '2002-06-05 00:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70116, 2197, 772, '<td valign="top">I think this subject would look excellent on a solid white surface.. the diagonals are nice, but the texture of the background surface make this photo seem a little ''busy'' to me...</td>', 'I think this subject would look excellent on a solid white surface.. the diagonals are nice, but the texture of the background surface make this photo seem a little ''busy'' to me...', '2002-06-05 00:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70117, 2197, 1528, '<td valign="top">nice shadows and textures</td>', 'nice shadows and textures', '2002-06-05 13:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70118, 2197, 472, '<td valign="top">the contrast and texture on this pic is unreal.  the arrangement is very pleasing as well.  the top left bead is a bit blown and unsharp so I give this an 8 : )</td>', 'the contrast and texture on this pic is unreal.  the arrangement is very pleasing as well.  the top left bead is a bit blown and unsharp so I give this an 8 : )', '2002-06-05 14:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70119, 2197, 885, '<td valign="top">Neat background</td>', 'Neat background', '2002-06-06 13:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70120, 2197, 1944, '<td valign="top">Seems to be a little over sharpened and contrasty. Good control of focus and exposure though.</td>', 'Seems to be a little over sharpened and contrasty. Good control of focus and exposure though.', '2002-06-06 20:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70121, 2197, 1005, '<td valign="top">Nice macro, great detail, love  your background, but a bit busy for the "coin" in the lower left corner, or maybe too similar color value.  The edges of the "coin" are clearly distinct, but because the color values are so similar, it wants to blend in slightly.   All the other elements work well.  Nice job!<br/>Photo 9 Creativity 8 B&amp;W 7 total 8</td>', 'Nice macro, great detail, love  your background, but a bit busy for the "coin" in the lower left corner, or maybe too similar color value.  The edges of the "coin" are clearly distinct, but because the color values are so similar, it wants to blend in slightly.   All the other elements work well.  Nice job!Photo 9 Creativity 8 B&W 7 total 8', '2002-06-07 16:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70122, 2197, 441, '<td valign="top">very strong contrasts and detail</td>', 'very strong contrasts and detail', '2002-06-07 19:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70123, 2197, 587, '<td valign="top">I really like the use of different textures, lighting and shadows - I prefer to see the whole image of things in a photo, but good job.</td>', 'I really like the use of different textures, lighting and shadows - I prefer to see the whole image of things in a photo, but good job.', '2002-06-08 21:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70124, 2197, 543, '<td valign="top">Excellent contrast and sharpness here - highlights are bright white, but detail is preserved, and the blacks are nice and dense.  Good choise of bg, too.  The diagonals add interest to the layout.  It does go ever so slightly soft at the bottom (don''t mind it at top).</td>', 'Excellent contrast and sharpness here - highlights are bright white, but detail is preserved, and the blacks are nice and dense.  Good choise of bg, too.  The diagonals add interest to the layout.  It does go ever so slightly soft at the bottom (don''t mind it at top).', '2002-06-09 04:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70125, 2197, 2091, '<td valign="top">Nice I like the lighting :)</td>', 'Nice I like the lighting :)', '2002-06-09 20:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70126, 2197, 1042, '<td valign="top">I voted this a 9. I wish it had placed higher. I really loved the textures and the fact that it shows only "parts" of the objects.  I just loved the contrast and the detail of this....sorry it didn''t do better.</td>', 'I voted this a 9. I wish it had placed higher. I really loved the textures and the fact that it shows only "parts" of the objects.  I just loved the contrast and the detail of this....sorry it didn''t do better.', '2002-06-10 10:59:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(70127, 2198, 1, '<td valign="top">I think some work needs to be done with your framing and centering.</td>', 'I think some work needs to be done with your framing and centering.', '2002-06-03 14:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70128, 2198, 203, '<td valign="top">On grey with a grey background.  Even the cracks in shadow are grey.  If this were the grey challenge you would be a contender.</td>', 'On grey with a grey background.  Even the cracks in shadow are grey.  If this were the grey challenge you would be a contender.', '2002-06-03 15:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70129, 2198, 772, '<td valign="top">nice cat!</td>', 'nice cat!', '2002-06-03 17:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70130, 2198, 327, '<td valign="top">Neat b&amp;w. Good job. Looks like he (she) is holding the pose for you. &amp;lt;lol&amp;gt; Nice cat, very pretty.</td>', 'Neat b&w. Good job. Looks like he (she) is holding the pose for you. &lt;lol&gt; Nice cat, very pretty.', '2002-06-03 18:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70131, 2198, 543, '<td valign="top">Good focus and nice textures from the available outdoor light.  Looks like an overcast day, which can produce vey nice, soft, portrait lighting.  Personally, I avoid shooting down on subjects unless the perspective is important to the image.  If that''s the perspective you wanted, I''d have tried to frame the image to exclude the grass.  You could still crop most of it out if you rotated the pic CCW a little.  A bit more contrast might help, as well.</td>', 'Good focus and nice textures from the available outdoor light.  Looks like an overcast day, which can produce vey nice, soft, portrait lighting.  Personally, I avoid shooting down on subjects unless the perspective is important to the image.  If that''s the perspective you wanted, I''d have tried to frame the image to exclude the grass.  You could still crop most of it out if you rotated the pic CCW a little.  A bit more contrast might help, as well.', '2002-06-04 04:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70132, 2198, 1041, '<td valign="top">What a cute cat, and great position.  I''m trying out a new "style" of critque, please let me know what you think.  IMO, what would''ve given your picture more impact is to have more contrast, getting rid of the grass in the background (the woodgrain and the cat are great for b&amp;w, the grass is not) and moving the cat out of the center of the photo.  I''ve taken the liberty to make a copy of your photo, crop it and increase the contrast.  What do you think?<br/><br/>//www.pbase.com/image/2359894<br/><br/>Of course you wouldn''t be able to crop it quite that same way for the challenge due to the sizing restrictions, but that''s where I would try to go with this shot.</td>', 'What a cute cat, and great position.  I''m trying out a new "style" of critque, please let me know what you think.  IMO, what would''ve given your picture more impact is to have more contrast, getting rid of the grass in the background (the woodgrain and the cat are great for b&w, the grass is not) and moving the cat out of the center of the photo.  I''ve taken the liberty to make a copy of your photo, crop it and increase the contrast.  What do you think?//www.pbase.com/image/2359894Of course you wouldn''t be able to crop it quite that same way for the challenge due to the sizing restrictions, but that''s where I would try to go with this shot.', '2002-06-04 09:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70133, 2198, 1882, '<td valign="top">oh god.  another cat picture.</td>', 'oh god.  another cat picture.', '2002-06-04 11:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70134, 2198, 811, '<td valign="top">That''s a very pretty cat, but I think the picture needs a little more contrast to it.  Maybe if the grass had been cropped out, and just the wood was the background, or if there had been something white or black nearby.</td>', 'That''s a very pretty cat, but I think the picture needs a little more contrast to it.  Maybe if the grass had been cropped out, and just the wood was the background, or if there had been something white or black nearby.', '2002-06-04 17:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(70135, 2198, 587, '<td valign="top">cute pose, colors seem too tame - IMO perhaps a bit more contrast would have helped.</td>', 'cute pose, colors seem too tame - IMO perhaps a bit more contrast would have helped.', '2002-06-05 00:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
